WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.000
Choose one of six offline books.
1,000 Cricket Facts by S Ballani is selected by default.

00:04.000 --> 00:09.000
Choose your mode, who bats first and the scoring page.
Either page allows every digit from 0 to 9.

00:09.000 --> 00:12.000
Close the book, then open it to play one ball.
On a flat iPhone, use the simulated book control.

00:12.000 --> 00:22.000
The highlighted last digit scores the ball.
Page 276 gives you six runs—and an aerial replay.

00:22.000 --> 00:32.000
Zero means a wicket.
The batsman misses and the bails fly off the stumps.

00:32.000 --> 00:36.000
An innings ends after five wickets or five overs.
The second side’s target is the first total plus one.

00:36.000 --> 00:40.000
Pass the phone and chase the target.
The current over and innings stay on the scorecard.

00:40.000 --> 00:46.000
Open Read facts from the home screen.
Search, pick a topic and follow each fact’s reference.
